=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: r11
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** FRR OSPF redistribution policy on R11 — specifically the `router ospf` stanza is missing the `redistribute eigrp 100` directive.

**Mechanism:** R11 sits at the EIGRP/OSPF boundary. Its OSPF process is configured with `redistribute connected`, which exports only R11's own directly-attached subnets (111.x, 112.x, 103.x) into the OSPF domain. EIGRP-learned routes for the wider EIGRP cloud — including the 120.0.0.0/8 LAN segment where pc12 lives — are never injected into OSPF LSAs. Consequently, every backbone router (R1, R2, R3, …) has a routing black hole for all EIGRP-cloud prefixes beyond R11's own links. When pc0 tries to reach 120.1.1.10, R1 (20.1.1.1) returns an immediate ICMP Destination Network Unreachable. When pc12 reaches out to 20.1.1.10, the forward path succeeds (EIGRP cloud has partial reachability through R11's connected redistributions), but R1 silently drops the ICMP reply — causing a full timeout on pc12.

**Localization:** R11, `router ospf` in FRR (`/etc/frr/frr.conf`). All physical interfaces (eth0 = EE domain to R12, eth1 = B domain to R1, eth2 = FF domain to R13) are UP with zero carrier errors; no link flap history exists.

**Root cause:** R11's OSPF process is missing `redistribute eigrp 100`, so the 120.0.0.0/8 subnet (and all other EIGRP-cloud prefixes) are never advertised into the OSPF backbone.

**Fix:** Add `redistribute eigrp 100` inside `router ospf` on R11. Symmetrically, add `redistribute ospf` inside `router eigrp 100` on R11 so that EIGRP-cloud routers (R12, R13) also learn backbone routes via R11, fully restoring two-way reachability.
=== END ===